5 Documentation work still required
The following topics need dedicated reference or how-to pages:

complete signatures, parameter semantics, return types, and exception tables for BITSZarrDataset, including inherited tensorbids methods;
a tested compatibility matrix for backend, transport, object store, and codec combinations;
format-specific authoring and reconstruction behavior for NIfTI, GIfTI, and CIfTI, including byte-fidelity limitations;
validation, freezing, integrity verification, failure recovery, and resumed ingestion;
cache sizing, concurrency, multiprocessing, and backend-specific performance guidance;
resolver conformance testing and extension guidance for libraries that implement additional BITS operators; and
a versioned on-disk layout and compatibility reference for dataset readers that do not use BITSZarrDataset.

1 Write the adapter
An adapter has a stable name and a scan(fs) method that returns a tensorbids.io.source.SourceManifest. This example handles a directory of &lt;subject&gt;.nii.gz T1-weighted images and a subjects.csv file:


flat_folder.py

from tensorbids.exceptions import UnrecognisedSource
from tensorbids.io.source import SkippedFile, SourceImage, SourceManifest


class FlatFolder:
    """A folder of &lt;subject&gt;.nii.gz T1w images, and subjects.csv."""

    name = "flat-folder"

    def scan(self, fs):
        found = {
            path.rsplit("/", 1)[-1]: info.size
            for path, info in fs.glob_info("*.nii.gz").items()
        }
        if not found:
            raise UnrecognisedSource(f"{fs.root}: no *.nii.gz images")
        images = tuple(
            SourceImage(
                path=path,
                target_path=f"sub-{s}/anat/sub-{s}_T1w.nii",
                format="nifti",
                sidecar={"Source": path},
            )
            for path in sorted(found)
            for s in [path.removesuffix(".nii.gz")]
        )
        return SourceManifest(
            adapter=self.name,
            description={"Name": "flat folder", "BIDSVersion": "1.10.0"},
            images=images,
            skipped=(SkippedFile("subjects.csv", "imported with write_table"),),
            sizes=found,
        )


Each SourceImage associates one source path with a valid BIDS target path and optional sidecar metadata.
sizes records the size of every consumed file, keyed by its path relative to the source root.
The manifest must account for each discovered file as imported, nested, or skipped with a reason.
Raise UnrecognisedSource when the source does not match the adapter’s expected layout.
